A||||9||Lewis||Cars stalls when I stop..plese help..||||8||
Z||000000||Lewis||03-26-2001||10:54 AM||||I have a 1985 gt with auto trans. The problem I am having is when I come to a stop (red light, stop sign) my car stalls out.  I am getting no codes when this happens. It sarts up alright but when it warms up it stalls..it runs okay also no hesitation and when I give it gas it also revs up alright. The rpm's drop to about 500 to 600 when this happens then stalls. It just started doing this out of the blue have had no other problems with the idle.  Any suggestions would be apprecited..lelwis||||reg||8
Z||000001||Tigger||03-26-2001||11:14 AM||||Sounds like a torque lockup solenoid problem.<P>Search the technical threads using <I>torque solenoid</I>.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lewis||03-26-2001||01:24 PM||||I took out my oxygen sensor and cleaned it a bit.  I just put this one in last summer.  Idle was high when i put it back in but i removed the battery cable and the idle is now at 800 and does not stall.  I also checked my egr and it is pretty rusted and broken.  When i pushed up on the inside the car wanted to stall and it almost got stuck had to tap on top of valve to release it.  Do you think this could be causing my idle problem?  Also where is the torque lockup selenoid located..maybe i should check this to see if it also causing a problem?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||Tigger||03-26-2001||02:12 PM||||Replace the EGR first.  My uncle had an automatic Indy Fiero where the EGR tube rusted and broke from the base.  Caused a real high erratic idle, you had to hold the gas and brake to keep it running.  Soon as we found the EGR was broke, we replaced it and it solved the problem.  Try that first, if it doesn't solve the stalling problem, get back with the forum.  <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||KRMFiero||03-26-2001||03:41 PM||||I was going to say push in the clutch but its automatic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>only think i can think of would be the torque converter lockup solenoid... my friends cavilier did that before, it was something wrong with the torque conveter solenoid i belive<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||03-26-2001||05:00 PM||||The connector for the torque converter solenoid is on the front side of the transmission (toward the firewall). It's a square plug. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000006||Lewis||03-27-2001||02:39 PM||||Changed egr and idle went back to normal.  The old egr was rusted out and just the stem was sticking out.  So far no more probs have to wait and see after I drive it for awhile. Thanks for all the suggestions. This forum is GREAT...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000007||shiloh187||03-27-2001||04:01 PM||||maybe this EGR is part of my problems.. where do i get a new one (what is one), and how much am i looking at?<P>shiloh<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||03-27-2001||04:05 PM||||Autozone $29||||reg||1
